  "disclosures": {
    "methodology": "<b>Window.</b> Comparison only includes calendar months where both endpoints fall inside the SPY TR series. The current overlap is <b>27 months (2.25y)</b>, Jan 31, 2024 → Apr 30, 2026.<br><br><b>Growth of $100,000.</b> Both lines start at $100,000 on the window-start date and chain monthly returns ($100K × ∏(1+Rᵢ)). SPY TR includes dividend reinvestment.<br><br><b>Drawdown.</b> Peak-to-trough percentage decline of the wealth index, computed independently for each line.<br><br><b>TWR.</b> Time-weighted return chains monthly Modified-Dietz returns and isolates investment performance from contribution timing.<br><br><b>IRR.</b> Money-weighted: same external cashflows, but the counterfactual buys SPY on each flow's date and rolls dividends — answers \"what if every contribution had gone into SPY instead?\".<br><br><b>Full portfolio.</b> Both TWR and IRR use the canonical compute_twr.py output with cross-account internal-transfer pairing applied portfolio-wide."
  },
